OL,3,GNEWSARapist's unpaid work sentence will
OL,4,Anot be reviewed
OL,5,
OL,6,FA decision to sentence a teenage rapist
OL,7,Fto unpaid work will not be reviewed by
OL,8,Fthe Attorney General's Office.
OL,10,FThomas Woodall, now aged 19, was found
OL,11,Fguilty of rape at Gloucester Crown
OL,12,FCourt. He was a handed a three-year
OL,13,Fcustody sentence, suspended for two
OL,14,Fyears.
OL,16,FThe Crown Prosecution Service wrote to
OL,17,Fthe Attorney General's Office to
OL,18,Frequest the sentence to be referred to
OL,19,Fthe Court of Appeal under the Unduly
OL,20,FLenient Sentence scheme, but the
OL,21,Frequest was rejected.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
